  "title": "RSLoRA: Training-free Rank Allocation for LoRA via Representational Sensitivity Probing",
  "summary": "RSLoRA (Representational Sensitivity LoRA) introduces a training-free, gradient-free rank allocator driven by activation-space geometry, effectively bridging the gap between expert heuristics and actual representational impact. It outperforms state-of-the-art allocators across mainstream benchmarks, demonstrating robustness and efficiency in large-scale model adaptation.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "RSLoRA eliminates the need for iterative training-time adjustments and backward gradients, achieving high efficiency.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "It identifies high-sensitivity modules requiring higher rank capacity through virtual representational probing and Effective Rank/Frechet Distance.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
